  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 1237 AM MDT Fri Aug 28 2026\n\nStrong southwesterly flow will develop over the region during the \nSAT-SUN-MON time frame. However, within this flow, it will be quite \nmoist as moisture will likely get picked up off the Pacific from the \nnumerous tropical cyclones which are occurring over this area along \nwith the typical monsoon flow which is ongoing. Based on this \npattern, the overall best chance of precip during this 3 day period \nwill be over the CONTDVD, especially across the San Juans. The \nplains may see a better chance of precip on Monday as a boundary is \nfcst to come down the plain, and the combo of the moisture aloft and \nenhanced upslope will allow for a better chance of precip on Monday \nover the lower elevations.\n\nSome of the precip over the CONTDVD during the SAT-SUN-MON time \nframe may be heavy, and flash flooding along the Divide may become a \nconcern.\n\nTemps on the plains SAT and SUN will be pushing around 100F over the \nplains along the lower Ark Rvr valley from Pueblo east to the KS \nborder. A bit cooler weather is expected on Monday.\n\nfrom TUE onward, SW flow aloft continues. Deterministic Models are \nin agreement with this flow pattern but differ a bit in how much \nmonsoon moisture will be caught up in the flow. Likewise, Mtns will \nlikely see the best chance of precip. NBM seems pretty dry over the \nmtns with sctd pops, with little if any precip plains. This to me \nlooks a bit underdone given the continued southwesterly flow aloft. \n\\/Hodanish",
